Job description
Sapient Logic has a career opening for a Senior-level Network Engineer to support&nbsp;the&nbsp;Joint Fires Network (JFN)&nbsp;program&nbsp;in San Diego, CA. At Sapient Logic, we welcome individuals who are open minded, think “outside the box”,&nbsp;and are eager to explore new challenges.&nbsp;


Responsibilities&nbsp;

- Design, configure, and install network infrastructure in support of customer requirements&nbsp;
- Configure and&nbsp;operate&nbsp;network switches, routers, and firewalls&nbsp;
- Design, implement, and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;enterprise SD-WAN solutions across different sites and cloud environments.&nbsp;
- Perform troubleshooting analysis of network infrastructure&nbsp;
- Create and implement network security measures&nbsp;
- Deal with escalated network support issues&nbsp;
- Generate network status reports&nbsp;
- Script network configurations via Ansible&nbsp;
- Conduct and&nbsp;monitor&nbsp;network performance (availability,&nbsp;utilization, throughput, and latency) and test for weaknesses&nbsp;
- Document internal processes and procedures related to duties and responsibilities&nbsp;
- Manage fellow network engineers and provide guidance on their respective duties&nbsp;


Skills&nbsp;

- A Bachelor’s&nbsp;degree with&nbsp;13&nbsp;years of IT Networking experience; OR an&nbsp;Associates&nbsp;degree and 15&nbsp;years of IT Networking experience; OR a High School Diploma/GED and&nbsp;17&nbsp;years of IT Networking experience is&nbsp;required&nbsp;
- Seven (7) years experience engineering network and/or firewall solutions for a DoW based system.
- CCNA&nbsp;certification.&nbsp;&nbsp;CCNP certification is preferred.&nbsp;&nbsp;
- Experience with Software Defined Network (SDN)&nbsp;
- Understanding of SDN and SD-WAN concepts and solutions and their deployment, including underlay/overlay, ISIS, VXLAN, DTLS, TLOC, policy development and enforcement, DNA Center,&nbsp;vManage/vBond/vSmart/vEdge&nbsp;
- Proficiency&nbsp;with SDN controllers like&nbsp;OpenDaylight, ONOS, and Cisco ACI&nbsp;
- Proficiency&nbsp;in Python&nbsp;
- Experience in Ansible is desired&nbsp;
- Experience with firewalls and Internet VPN’s remote implementation&nbsp;
- In-depth understanding of&nbsp;and ability to implement/troubleshoot&nbsp;Cisco QoS (classification, marking, shaping, policing)&nbsp;
- In-depth knowledge of dynamic routing protocols and switching technologies such as EIGRP, BGP, OSPF, HSRP, NHRP, GRE, DMVPN,&nbsp;PAgP, LACP, VTP, CDP, CEF, VLANS, STP, OTV, TACACS, Radius, NetFlow, QoS, 802.1x&nbsp;
- Ability to troubleshoot complex routing and switching issues in both a LAN / WAN environment&nbsp;
- Ability to manage fellow engineers&nbsp;
- OPERATING SYSTEMS: Linux, Windows 10, Windows Server 2016 or greater&nbsp;
- HARDWARE: Cisco switches, routers, and firewalls&nbsp;
- DoD TS/SCI Clearance&nbsp;is&nbsp;required&nbsp;
- U.S. Citizenship is&nbsp;required&nbsp;


Job Type: Full-time&nbsp;
Benefits:&nbsp;

- 401(k)&nbsp;
- 401(k) matching&nbsp;
- Dental insurance&nbsp;
- Employee&nbsp;assistance&nbsp;program&nbsp;
- Employee discount&nbsp;
- Flexible spending account&nbsp;
- Health insurance&nbsp;
- Health savings account&nbsp;
- Life insurance&nbsp;
- Paid time off&nbsp;
- Parental leave&nbsp;
- Professional development&nbsp;assistance&nbsp;
- Referral program&nbsp;
- Retirement plan&nbsp;
- Vision insurance&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Schedule:&nbsp;

- 8 hour&nbsp;shift&nbsp;
- Monday to Friday&nbsp;
Experience:&nbsp;

- Computer networking: 6 years (Required)&nbsp;
- WAN: 3 years (Preferred)&nbsp;
License/Certification:&nbsp;

- At least CCNA.&nbsp;CCNP (Preferred)&nbsp;
Security clearance:&nbsp;

- TS/SCI (Required)&nbsp;
Work Location: In person&nbsp;
Salary: $180,000 - $200,000
&nbsp;

